From: Win7 port restore
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] desktop: pin Electron 22.3.27 (last Win7-capable major)

Electron 23+ drops Windows 7/8/8.1 support. 22.3.27 is the final 22.x
release (Chromium 108 / Node 16.17) and the GUI runtime used by the Win7
build. Pin it exactly (no caret) so electronDist resolution and the
renderer baseline (Chromium 108 CSS support, see patch 002) stay stable.

electron-builder is pinned to 26.8.1 because patch 006 patches
app-builder-lib code paths whose line positions differ between versions.

`npmRebuild: false` is already present upstream (desktop builds never
rebuild node-pty on Linux); no change needed there.

--- a/desktop/package.json
+++ b/desktop/package.json
@@ -145,8 +145,8 @@
     "@typescript-eslint/parser": "^8",
     "@vitejs/plugin-react": "^6.0.1",
     "@vitest/coverage-v8": "3.2.4",
-    "electron": "^42.4.0",
-    "electron-builder": "^26.8.1",
+    "electron": "22.3.27",
+    "electron-builder": "26.8.1",
     "eslint": "^9",
     "eslint-plugin-react-hooks": "^5",
     "jsdom": "^25.0.1",
